From e3c88fb2ca1c09f649006af99af39496242dfc0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ren=C3=A9=20Rebe?= <rene@exactco.de>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:49:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] powerpc: Restore the PReP platform
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Revert 933ee7119fb1 ("powerpc: remove PReP platform") and b858a97bf053
("vga16fb: drop powerpc support") and port the PowerPC Reference Platform
support of the former arch/ppc to arch/powerpc, primarily for the Motorola
PowerStack (Blackhawk).

Bootwrapper, dtbImage.prep:
 - the firmware loads the image anywhere and enters it with r3 pointing to
   the residual data; prep-head.S copies that while still in the firmware's
   MMU state (OpenBIOS enters translated), drops to real mode with the data
   cache off, so ISA I/O at 0x80000000 is not cached, and moves the image to
   its link address, kept above the kernel including its bss
 - prep.c sizes memory from the MPC105/106/107 or the residual data, sets the
   CPU clocks and timebase, passes the residual data as /prep,residual-data
   and takes bootargs from the PReP NVRAM
 - mkprep writes the bootable 0x41 partition image

Platform:
 - residual data from the device tree, bounds checked by its length, for the
   PCI config method, PCI interrupts, IRQ sense and the 8259 interrupt
   acknowledge address, exported as /proc/residual
 - PCI host bridge at discover_phbs time, the legacy ISA ports are mapped
   early from the device tree ranges for i8259 and board setup
 - Motorola and IBM board PCI IRQ tables and SIO PIRQ/ELCR programming
 - timebase from the device tree, or calibrated against the RTC
 - M48T59 (Motorola) or MC146818 (IBM) RTC platform devices
 - L2 enable, restart via port 92, IBM Signetics 87c750 power off

Adapted to the current tree: 6xx is PPC_BOOK3S_32 and PPC_NATIVE is
PPC_HASH_MMU_NATIVE, Documentation/powerpc moved to Documentation/arch/powerpc,
maple is not re-added.  The powerpc screen_info global, the TASK_SIZE default
and the cirrusfb PReP address hack are not restored; the latter two relied on
the arch/ppc fixed I/O block mappings.

Motorola Raven/Hawk boards with OpenPIC and SMP are not supported.

Tested with QEMU -M 40p through the OpenBIOS PReP boot.  The Motorola board
paths have not run yet.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
